88
00:02:32,190 --> 00:02:35,250
it's very common nowadays that a single processor

89
00:02:35,250 --> 00:02:37,930
actually contains multiple cores,

90
00:02:37,930 --> 00:02:40,890
or that there are simply multiple processors.

91
00:02:40,890 --> 00:02:44,450
In that case, this is actually the most common

92
00:02:44,450 --> 00:02:46,870
form of concurrent multitasking.

93
00:02:46,870 --> 00:02:49,130
As you can see up here,

94
00:02:49,130 --> 00:02:49,970
there are two —

95
00:02:49,970 --> 00:02:51,110
say, two processors,

96
00:02:51,110 --> 00:02:52,430
and on each processor,

97
00:02:52,430 --> 00:02:54,250
one control flow is running respectively.

98
00:02:54,250 --> 00:02:55,810
Between them,

99
00:02:55,810 --> 00:02:57,070
they are completely independent,

100
00:02:57,070 --> 00:02:58,290
with no interaction whatsoever

101
00:02:58,290 --> 00:02:59,010
without any interference.

102
00:02:59,010 --> 00:03:01,370
Now, in modern computer

103
00:03:01,370 --> 00:03:02,310
architectures,

104
00:03:02,310 --> 00:03:04,390
this is called

105
00:03:04,390 --> 00:03:08,550
